    <!-- ================= 11. TOPICS ================= -->
    <section class="topics-section" id="topics">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-head center" data-anim="fade-up">
                <span class="eyebrow">How Sohba was engineered</span>
                <h2>From solid foundations to production-grade systems.</h2>
                <p>Every concept below is implemented in the codebase — not a checklist, a build log.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="topics-grid" data-anim="fade-up">
                <div class="topics-col">
                    <div class="topics-col-head foundations">
                        <div class="badge"><i data-lucide="layers"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <h3>Foundations</h3>
                            <span>The architecture everything else stands on</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="topic-list">
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Clean / layered architecture</strong> — Domain, Application, Infrastructure, and Web kept strictly separate.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>ASP.NET Core MVC &amp; Razor Views</strong> — server-rendered pages with AJAX-aware controllers.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Entity Framework Core</strong> — code-first modelling with Fluent API configurations.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>ASP.NET Core Identity</strong> — role-based authorization for Users, Admins, and Owners.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Repository &amp; Unit of Work</strong> — a consistent data-access boundary across every feature.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>DTOs &amp; AutoMapper</strong> — domain entities never leak directly into views.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>FluentValidation</strong> — declarative, testable input rules on every form.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="topics-col">
                    <div class="topics-col-head advanced">
                        <div class="badge"><i data-lucide="cpu"></i></div>
                        <div>
                            <h3>Advanced engineering</h3>
                            <span>What makes Sohba feel production-grade</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="topic-list">
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>SignalR real-time hubs</strong> — authenticated over a JWT handshake, not just a demo chat.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Domain-driven business rules</strong> — dedicated domain services enforce privacy and depth limits.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Soft-delete via global query filters</strong> — deleted data disappears everywhere, instantly, by design.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Filtered SQL indexes</strong> — uniqueness enforced only on active pending requests.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Policy-based rate limiting</strong> — eight partitioned windows tuned per endpoint risk.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Background hosted services</strong> — hourly story cleanup, daily notification pruning.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Image pipeline with rollback</strong> — magic-byte checks, WebP re-encoding, automatic cleanup on failure.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Protected out-of-webroot media</strong> — story files streamed only after a live authorization check.</div></div>
                        <div class="topic-item"><span class="dot"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg></span><div><strong>Immutable audit logging</strong> — every admin action recorded, with lineage protection built in.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= 12. SHIP-READY ================= -->
    <section class="shipready-section" id="shipready">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-head center" data-anim="fade-up">
                <span class="eyebrow">Ship-ready</span>
                <h2>Engineering practices you can verify, not promises.</h2>
                <p>Sohba ships with the tooling that keeps a codebase honest — automated tests, continuous integration, and a reproducible deployment stack.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ship-grid">
                <div class="ship-card" data-anim="reveal">
                    <div class="ship-icon"><i data-lucide="flask-conical"></i></div>
                    <h3>Tested where it matters</h3>
                    <p>Self-contained xUnit suites cover the domain rules and application services — including refresh-token rotation and reuse detection — with no database required to run them.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ship-card" data-anim="reveal">
                    <div class="ship-icon"><i data-lucide="git-branch"></i></div>
                    <h3>CI on every push</h3>
                    <p>A GitHub Actions workflow builds the Release configuration and runs both test projects on every push and pull request to master.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="ship-card" data-anim="reveal">
                    <div class="ship-icon"><i data-lucide="container"></i></div>
                    <h3>One-command deployment</h3>
                    <p><code>docker compose up</code> starts the full stack — MVC app + SQL Server 2022 — with auto-applied migrations and persistent volumes for data, uploads, and logs.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

